\section{Known limitations}{

\itemize{
\item The predicted quantity is the surrogate scored against the oracle's
predictions, which can differ in level and plateau from the original
surrogate-vs-test-set target (inherent to a self-contained forecast).
\item Search-space transformations are ignored: the oracle is fit on, and
proposals are made on, the untransformed scale.
\item \code{se} reflects only proposer/sampler stochasticity across restarts; a
deterministic configuration yields \code{se = 0}.
}
